# ClaudeSwitch signing / notarization credentials.
#
# Copy this file to scripts/signing.env (gitignored) and fill in your own
# values. build-dmg.sh sources signing.env automatically when present. Without
# it, the build still runs and produces an ad-hoc–signed (unsigned) DMG —
# fine for local install; distribution and --publish require real credentials.
#
# All values may also be supplied via the environment instead of this file.

# Reverse-DNS bundle identifier for the app.
# BUNDLE_ID="com.irvcassio.ClaudeSwitch"

# Apple Developer Team ID (10-char).
# TEAM_ID="8B3CHTY93V"

# Codesigning identity as shown by `security find-identity -v -p codesigning`.
# SIGN_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Irven Cassio (8B3CHTY93V)"

# notarytool keychain profile name (see `xcrun notarytool store-credentials`).
# NOTARY_PROFILE="my-notary-profile"

# Apple ID email used for notarization.
# NOTARY_APPLE_ID="you@example.com"

# Team ID for notarization (defaults to TEAM_ID if unset).
# NOTARY_TEAM_ID="8B3CHTY93V"

# ── Auto-update (Sparkle) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate ONE EdDSA keypair for THIS app with Sparkle's generate_keys:
#   generate_keys --account claudeswitch
# It MUST be ClaudeSwitch's own pair — not Doppo Terminal's, not Doppo
# Browser's, not Canopy's. A shared key means compromising one product forges
# updates for all of them, with no way to rotate one without breaking the
# others. The private key signs the appcast; the public key is embedded in
# Info.plist as SUPublicEDKey. The variable holds a PATH to the exported key
# file, never the key material itself.
# SPARKLE_PRIVATE_KEY="$HOME/.doppo-signing/claudeswitch-sparkle-ed25519.key"
# SPARKLE_PUBLIC_KEY="<base64 public key>"

# Local checkout of irvcassio/doppoworks — the publish target for the feed
# (`build-dmg.sh --publish`). Default: ~/doppoworks
# SITE_REPO="$HOME/doppoworks"

# ── Publish targets (only used with --publish) ───────────────────────────────
# Public repo that hosts the DMG as a release asset, so Sparkle can download
# the binary unauthenticated.
# RELEASE_REPO="irvcassio/app-downloads"
#
# Release tag shape: <prefix><marketing>-b<build>.
# RELEASE_TAG_PREFIX="claudeswitch-v"
#
# Which directory under the site repo's public/downloads/ holds THIS product's
# appcast.xml. Pointing it at another product's directory would offer
# ClaudeSwitch as an update to every install of that one.
# FEED_DIR="claudeswitch"
